From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: disable lid debounce for the
 EINT test

The lid produced no interrupt in two boots. gpio-keys sets debounce
before requesting its dual-edge interrupt, and mtk-eint enables hardware
debounce when the line is still level-sensitive from the loader. The
vendor EINT driver never debounces an edge-sensitive line.

Request no debounce for the lid so the next test separates this from a
pin level that never changes. Bounce is acceptable for a single
attended close/open.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
index 8d91a299b..d781f5121 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -548,7 +548,12 @@ hall-switch {
 			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
 			linux,code = <SW_LID>;
 			gpios = <&pio 66 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-			debounce-interval = <64>;
+			/*
+			 * No debounce: mtk-eint would enable hardware debounce
+			 * from the loader's level setting before the line is
+			 * switched to dual edge.
+			 */
+			debounce-interval = <0>;
 		};
 	};
 };
